Softgel Manufacturing Equipment market was valued at US$ 85.90 million in 2024 and is projected to reach US$ 129.30 million by 2031, growing at a steady CAGR of 6.6% during the forecast period (2025-2031). This expansion is driven by escalating demand for pharmaceutical softgels, nutraceutical supplements, and the growing preference for gelatin-based encapsulation across healthcare sectors.

What is Softgel Manufacturing Equipment?
Softgel manufacturing equipment comprises specialized machinery designed for producing soft gelatin capsules - a preferred dosage form for pharmaceuticals and supplements. These systems handle the complete production cycle including material preparation, encapsulation, drying, inspection, and packaging. The technology ensures precise dosing, hermetic sealing of liquid/semi-solid formulations, and maintains stringent GMP compliance for pharmaceutical applications.

Modern softgel machines integrate automation, IoT sensors for quality control, and can produce 30,000-100,000 capsules/hour in industrial settings. They've become indispensable for manufacturers of omega-3 supplements, vitamin formulations, and prescription drugs requiring bioavailability enhancement.

